<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  New file: the iOS target had no entitlements at all — only CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS[sdk=macosx*]
  existed, so iOS was signed with none.

  ## The app group, previously omitted on purpose and now declared

  This file used to say the group was deliberately absent, because declaring it changes behaviour:
  `SharedStore` calls `UserDefaults(suiteName:)`, which returned nil on iOS and fell back to
  `.standard`. That was the correct call while nothing needed it.

  The planetary-hours widget needs it. A widget extension has its **own** bundle and therefore its
  own `.standard`, so under the old fallback the app wrote the observer's place into the *app's*
  defaults and the widget read an empty *extension's* defaults — the location could never cross the
  process boundary, and any place-dependent widget would render its no-place state forever.

  Nothing migrates. `ChartViewModel` keeps the authoritative copy under its own keys in `.standard`
  and calls `syncShared()` at init and on every location change, so the group container is
  populated on first launch after this ships. The two stores use identical key names
  (`observerLatitude`, `houseSystem`, …) and were literally the same store on iOS until now.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.oleksandr.aisixteen.ephemeris</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudDocuments</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.oleksandr.aisixteen.ephemeris</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.oleksandr.aisixteen.ephemeris</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
